  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "Knowing times tables up to 10 × 10 makes harder math much faster."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "Division is the opposite of multiplication: if 6 × 7 = 42, then 42 ÷ 7 = 6."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "For big multiplication, split numbers: 23 × 4 = (20 × 4) + (3 × 4) = 80 + 12 = 92."
    },
    {
      "type": "fact",
      "body": "Trick for 9s: 9 × 7 = 63, and 6 + 3 = 9. The digits of the 9 times table (up to 9 × 10) always add to 9!"
    }
  ],
